01 plan-writer done [11.8m 101 turns $4.16 · opus · default]: The plan (521 lines) builds gh-3. Auth: one `auth/names.py` holds every name rule (trim, NFC, the refused Unicode categories and the default-ignorable ranges, the case-folded key, suffixes, and the migration's `dedupe`). Uniqueness is a stored `display_name_key` under one unique index, so the app and the database compare the same value, and that index also settles the races. A one-way migration 0002 normalises and renames duplicates, 0003 adds `user_preferences` with an atomic jsonb upsert merge, and the routes follow D28/D46. SPA: a `/settings` page inside the shell; on success a rename updates the session profile and every directory cache from the mutation's own `onSuccess`, so it still lands after the page unmounts; the clock reaches all three formatters through `ClockProvider`, with an optimistic save that reverts on failure. The test approach is BDD outside-in with the one Alan journey the issue names, and everything else is unit, integration or Vitest. One correction to the issue: sign-in does not return to the route it started from, so the plan builds that for every protected route. 12 decisions are marked assumed (case folding, code-point length, the IdP base name, suffix truncation, empty stored names, PATCH {}, sign-in return path, Back to chat, client-side Save gating, the late-failure rule for the clock, and two more).
